                        <del rend="erasure">בפלג</del>
                        <add place="superimposed">ה</add>
                    </mod> בכל נכסנ זי יהוונ בינ <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> ו<persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165">תמת</persName><lb n="12" rend="right-to-left" />מחר או יומ אחרנ תמות <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165">תמת</persName>
                    <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> הו ^הו^ שליט <del rend="erasure">בפלג</del> בכל נכסנ זי יהוונ בינ <del rend="erasure">בינ</del><lb n="13" rend="right-to-left" /><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165">תמת</persName> ובינ <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> ואנה <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p3025">משלמ</persName> מחר או יומ אחרנ לא אכל אנצל ל<persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20170">פלטי</persName> מנתחת<lb n="14" rend="right-to-left" />לבבכ בר מנ זי אנת תתר<add place="in space">כ</add> לאמה <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165">תמת</persName>
                    <add place="above">והנ הנצלתה מנכ אנתנ ל<persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> כספ כרשנ 111 11</add> כתב <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20175">נתנ בר ענניה</persName> ספרא זנה ושהדיא<lb n="15" rend="right-to-left" />בגו שהד <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20180">נתנ בר גדול<handShift cert="low" new="ancient_persons.xml#p20180" /></persName>
                    <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20185">מנחמ בר זכור<handShift cert="high" new="ancient_persons.xml#p20185" /></persName>
                    <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20190">גמריה בר מחסיה<handShift cert="high" new="ancient_persons.xml#p20190" /></persName></ab>
                <ab xml:lang="Armi arc"><pb n="V" /><lb n="vso 1" rend="right-to-left" />הנעלת <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165">תמת</persName> ל<persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> בידה כספ כרש 1 שקלנ 111 11 <note>Line comfirming money exchanged on top of verso</note><space dim="vertical" extent="unknown" unit="lines" /><lb n="vso 2" rend="right-to-left" />ספר א<supplied evidence="previouseditor" reason="lost">נתו זי כתב <persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20035">ענני</persName> ל</supplied><persName ref="ancient_persons.xml#p20165"><supplied evidence="previouseditor" reason="lost">ת</supplied>מת</persName><note>Endorsement at bottom of verso.</note></ab>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" >
                <ab xml:lang="Latn en">
                    <pb n="V" />
                <lb n="1" rend="left-to-right" />[On] the 18th of [Ab, that is day 30 ]⸢of⸣ the month of Pharmuthi, year 16 of Artaxer(xes) the king, said 
                <lb n="2" rend="left-to-right" />ˁAnanyah son of ˁAzaryah, a lḥn-servitor of Yahô the God, who is in Fort Elephantine, to Mešullam son of Zakkûr, an Aramean of Syene 
                <lb n="3" rend="left-to-right" />of the detachment of Varyazata, saying: I came to you (m.s.) (asking you) to give me ⸢the one named⸣ Tamet, ⸢who is your (m.s.) female-servant⸣, for wifehood. She is my wife 
                <lb n="4" rend="left-to-right" />and I am her husband from this day and forever. Tamet brought into me in her hand: garment of wool–1, equal (in) silver (to)
                <lb n="5" rend="left-to-right" />7 šeqels; mirror–1, equal (in) silver to 7 (and) a half hallurs; pair of sandals–1; balsam oil– (erased: 1 handful) 
                <lb n="6" rend="left-to-right" />half a handful; castor oil–6 handfuls; tray–1. Total of the silver and the value of the goods (in) silver = silver, 7 šeqels
                <lb n="7" rend="left-to-right" />7 (and) a half hallurs. Should tomorrow or another day, ˁAnanî stand in an assembly and say: “I hated Tamet my wife,”
                <lb n="8" rend="left-to-right" />the silver of a hater is on his head. He shall give Tamet silver, 7 (and) \2 q(uarters)/ ṯeqels, and all that she brought in in her hand she shall take out, from straw 
                <lb n="9" rend="left-to-right" />to string. Should tomorrow or another day, should Tamet stand and say: “I hated my husband ˁAnanî,” the silver of a hater is on her head. 
                <lb n="10" rend="left-to-right" />She shall give ˁAnanî silver, 7 shekels (and) \2 q(uarters)/ and all that she brought in in her hand she shall take out, from straw to string. Should tomorrow or 
                <lb n="11" rend="left-to-right" />another (10) day, (11) ˁAnanyah die, Tamet, she (errasure: Mešullam son of Zaccur, he] has right (errasure: to half) to all goods which will be between ˁAnanî and Tamet. 
                <lb n="12" rend="left-to-right" />Should tomorrow or or another day, Tamet die, ˁAnanî, he \he/ has right (ERASURE: to half) to all goods which will be between (ERASURE: between) 
                <lb n="13" rend="left-to-right" />Tamet and between ˁAnanî. And I, Meshullam, tomorrow or another day, shall not be able to reclaim Pilṭî from under 
                <lb n="14" rend="left-to-right" />your (m.s.) (legal) satisfaction unless you expel his mother Tamet. \And if I have reclaimed him from you (m.s.), I shall give ˁAnanî silver, 5 karsh./ Wrote Natan son of ˁAnanyah this document. And the witnesses 
                <lb n="15" rend="left-to-right" />herein: witness, Natan son of Gaddûl; Menaḥem son of Zakkûr; Gemaryah son of Maḥseyah.
                </ab>
                    <ab xml:lang="Latn en"><pb n="V" />
                <lb n="1" rend="left-to-right" />Tamet brought in to ˁAnanî in her hand silver, 1 karsh, 5 shekels.
                <lb n="2" rend="left-to-right" />⸢Do⸣cument of wi[fehood which ˁAnanî wrote for Ta]⸢m⸣et.
                    </ab>
            </div>
